The gnome warlock Pipwick crept through Stranglethorn Vale, his succubus pet, Vexia, shimmering beside him. Bandits lurked in the shadows, but Vexia’s charm kept them pacified. Pipwick grinned. “You’re the best leveling pet,” he said. Vexia smirked. “I know.” They cleared a camp, looted, and moved on. Then a patrol of murlocs appeared. Vexia sighed. “I can’t seduce fish people.” Pipwick nodded. “That’s why I keep a voidwalker for dungeons.” Vexia rolled her eyes. “But I’m prettier.” Pipwick laughed. “And that’s why everyone thinks you’re everywhere.”

**Answer:** Succubus has **Seduction**, which charms humanoids, making it seem like more warlocks use it than actually do. In reality, most level with voidwalkers because Seduction is situational, while voidwalkers tank better and are more reliable for general questing. The perceived popularity comes from the fact that when a warlock *does* use Seduction, it’s very visible—charmed mobs follow you around, making it look like succubus is the standard. [end of text]


